rustscrapling is a Rust port of Scrapling, a Python web-scraping library. Large
parts of this crate are derived from Scrapling: the adaptive element
fingerprinting and relocation algorithm, the similarity scoring used by
find_similar, the ::text and ::attr pseudo-element handling, the selector
generation, the crawl scheduler and request fingerprinting, the AutoThrottle
delay formula, the link extractor, and the Chromium launch-flag lists.

Those portions remain subject to the BSD 3-Clause License reproduced below. The
MIT License of this crate applies to the original Rust work; it does not and
cannot relicense the Scrapling material.

