Scrapling's CSS-to-XPath translator states that it is an adapted version of
parsel's translator, and Scrapling depends on w3lib for URL canonicalization,
HTML entity replacement, and the default ignored-extensions list. Where
rustscrapling reimplements that behaviour (canonicalize_url, the
IGNORED_EXTENSIONS set, entity replacement, and the ::text / ::attr
pseudo-element semantics), the lineage traces to those projects.

